Implement a self-contained TypeScript module exporting `RouteDescriptor` and `RouteEndpoint`:

```typescript
export interface RouteDescriptor {
  scheme: string;
  host: string;
  port: number;
  accountId: number;
  groupId: number;
}

export class RouteEndpoint {
  public constructor(descriptor: RouteDescriptor);
  public getDescriptor(): RouteDescriptor;
  public toString(): string;
}
```

The constructor must reject with `TypeError` if `scheme` or `host` is empty, if either identifier is not a non-negative safe integer, or if `port` is not an integer from 1 through 65535. Whitespace-only strings are not empty and must be preserved verbatim. Copy the descriptor; later changes to the argument must not affect the instance. `getDescriptor` must return a fresh object so callers cannot mutate internal state. `toString` must return `<scheme>://<host>:<port> [account=<accountId>, group=<groupId>]` without normalization or encoding.

